{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, thanks for reaching out. I'd like to help, but I need a few details to find the problem. Could you tell me: 1) What happens on your computer (for example freezing, slow apps, a error message, a blue screen, or something else)? 2) What was the exact message or error, if you saw one? 3) When did it start, and did it happen after a Windows update or a new app install? 4) When did you last restart your laptop (a full restart, not just closing the lid)? Once I have these, I can continue troubleshooting. Your laptop BL-LT-0107 is showing offline and hasn't checked in for 12 days, so please also tell me whether it's been turned on and connected to the network recently.",
  "internal_note": "Triage was vague ('the thing again'). Looked up user 7 (Sofia Rossi, Marketing, active, not locked, no failed logins, VPN enabled). Sole device BL-LT-0107 (Win 11 Pro): offline, last check-in 2026-09-29 (12 days ago), warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Disk healthy at 54.7% free (140 GB), so KB-017 does not apply. No symptoms reported, so KB-019 quick checks are pending user answers (last restart, recent updates/installs). Asked user for symptoms, error text, timing, last restart. Possible follow-up: if the laptop was off or disconnected, that may explain the gap and needs a check on whether it is in use. Not escalating yet because no specific fault has been described. Confidence low until details arrive.",
